+## Keys and roles
+
+Every request carries `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Keys are the `apiKeys`
+of the data file (`docs/DATA.md`); each has one role:
+
+- `viewer`: read only (every `GET` route except `GET /audit`).
+- `cook`: also `POST /recipes/:id/cook`, `POST /batches/:id/waste`,
+  `POST /temperatures` and `POST /stocktakes/:id/counts`.
+- `manager`: everything, including `GET /audit`.
+
+No key or an unknown key answers 401 `unauthorized` (also for routes that do
+not exist); a known key whose role is too low answers 403 `forbidden`.
+
+## Audit
+
+Every request other than a `GET` that comes with a known key writes an audit
+entry, whether it succeeded or not (a refused or failed attempt is recorded
+with its status). `GET /audit` lists the entries newest first, for managers:
+
+    { "id": 1, "at": "2026-10-28T10:00:00.000Z", "keyName": "cook-dev",
+      "method": "POST", "path": "/recipes/1/cook", "status": 200 }
+
 ## Errors

 Errors have a status from `src/errors.js` and the body
